          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "bretelle was borrowed from Old High German brittil 'rein, strap' (EtymDB). A strap ties two things together, and so does a short road between two big ones."
            }
          ]
        },
